reader-env
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: `!Reader.env` inside a direct block — ask whose environment type
  is taken from the BLOCK'S ROW, so nothing is named twice and no local
  alias is needed. Two witnesses resolved at typer time: `RowOf[F]`
  recovers the row from the block's program type, `EnvOf[R]` finds the
  Reader's environment inside it. `env` must be `inline`: the DirectCtx
  that pins F is a value parameter, and the macro strips the context
  lambda, so a surviving reference to it is a dangling parameter —
  inline makes the parameter disappear at expansion and leaves
  `Reader.ask[E]`.
files: src/main/scala/Reader.scala, src/test/scala/TestReaderHas.scala,
  docs/typepedia.md, CHANGELOG.md
